    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Luk Fu (Six Tigers)',
            subtitle: 'Six Tigers',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Luk Fu (å…­è™Ž), literally 'Six Tigers', is a traditional Hakka Chinese trick-taking game played with a unique money-suited deck of 38 cards. It is a highly complex and fast-paced game where players compete to be the first to capture six 'Fu' (tigers/tricks). The game features 'Aged Cards' (cards that become unbeatable) and special multi-trick combinations like 'Five Tigers Emerge From the Mountain' (Ng Fu Ha San).",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Dates back centuries to the Hakka people in Southern China. It is related to other money-suited games like Khanhoo and Madiao.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '3 active players (one can be a dummy dealer in a 4-player game).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '38 cards: 4 suits (Coins, Strings, Myriads, Tens). Each suit has 1-9. Plus special Aces.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Chinese money-suited deck and score counters.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Each player receives 12 cards (in a 3-player game).',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'Four-Player Luk Fu: One player pays but does not play.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Small Fu: A variant requiring only 5 tricks.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Hakka Lucky Tiger: A gambling-heavy variant.',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
    description: "Luk Fu (å…­è™Ž), literally 'Six Tigers', is a traditional Hakka Chinese trick-taking game played with a unique money-suited deck of 38 cards. It is a highly complex and fast-paced game where players compete to be the first to capture six 'Fu' (tigers/tricks). The game features 'Aged Cards' (cards that become unbeatable) and special multi-trick combinations like 'Five Tigers Emerge From the Mountain' (Ng Fu Ha San).",
