          deckDescription: 'A 38-card Hakka money-suited deck. Thirty-six cards are used in play: four suits (Tens/Sup, Myriads/Gong, Knots/Sok, Coins/Tyen) with ranks 1 to 9 each, plus five Aces (one per suit and an Extra Ace). The 38th card is not used. Suit order for trick purposes: Tens high, then Myriads, Knots, Coins low.',
          suitDescription: 'Four money suits: Tens (Sup, ranking high), Myriads (Gong), Knots (Sok), and Coins (Tyen, ranking low). Each suit has ranks 1 through 9. Aces are the fifth rank per suit; the Extra Ace has no suit.',
          rankDescription: 'Ranks 1 (low) to 9 (high) in each suit. The four Nines and Aces of Tens and Coins (and the Extra Ace if in play) are Old Cards (Lao Sui Pai), initially unbeatable. Cards become Old when known to be the highest remaining in their suit.',
